  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 116.0,
  "event_seq": 269,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to 1180-1260/month in Aug-Sep 2026 (E-07). Of the 1240 ESTIMATED-read disputed bills (out of 3025 total, E-04), 1184 are AMI reads that arrived on time and were exported to billing but were rejected at import with billing_import_status=REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION, not missed field routes or AMI non-arrival (only 56 were true non-arrivals) (E-11). This coincides with billing-config rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, which compares raw meter register values directly against 12-month m3 consumption history with no unit scaling (E-12), while AMI firmware v4.2 (rolled out 2026-06) reports registers in units of 0.1 m3 rather than m3 (E-13) - so genuine, on-time reads from v4.2 meters are misread as abnormal high consumption, rejected, and billed as estimates, driving the estimate-substitution bucket of the dispute surge."
 },
